WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
Every test corpus of any size has the same problem.

00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:06.040
You can run everything, or you can run one thing.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:10.680
Running exactly the right subset, and being able to prove later which subset

00:00:10.680 --> 00:00:12.600
that was, is the awkward part.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:14.200
Tags help.

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:18.540
Until the tag query lives in a CI job parameter that nobody can

00:00:18.540 --> 00:00:19.880
reconstruct three weeks later.

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:23.080
runcomposer splits that problem in two.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.880
Composing the selection is a first-class, reviewable act that produces a document.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:31.800
Executing it is somebody else's job, deliberately so.

00:00:32.760 --> 00:00:33.800
That is the thesis.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.240
The interface is a document, not a protocol.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:39.627
It starts with a catalog.

00:00:40.207 --> 00:00:46.087
A test source enumerates your tests as items, an opaque, stable ID, plus tags.

00:00:46.607 --> 00:00:49.567
Then it content hashes the whole catalog into a snapshot.

00:00:50.527 --> 00:00:52.667
The ID space belongs to the source.

00:00:53.247 --> 00:00:56.647
A robot framework source mints IDs from suite longnames.

00:00:57.227 --> 00:01:03.007
A manifest source takes a plain JSON list, so a pytest corpus arrives as node ids.

00:01:03.967 --> 00:01:05.827
The core never parses an ID.

00:01:05.827 --> 00:01:09.047
It compares IDs for equality, and that is all.

00:01:10.233 --> 00:01:11.613
Now compose.

00:01:11.613 --> 00:01:15.693
Navigate the taxonomy, a curated tree over tag patterns,

00:01:15.693 --> 00:01:17.553
data rather than code.

00:01:17.553 --> 00:01:21.693
Build a filter and watch the preview recompile as you type.

00:01:21.693 --> 00:01:24.293
The filter language is deliberately small.

00:01:24.293 --> 00:01:26.753
A bare word is a literal tag.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:30.153
A prefix pattern is sugar for an anchored regular expression.

00:01:30.153 --> 00:01:32.493
And regex is the escape hatch.

00:01:32.493 --> 00:01:36.353
Three operators, and, or, not.

00:01:36.353 --> 00:01:38.153
Small but lossless.

00:01:38.153 --> 00:01:40.953
The filter stays a tree, and that tree survives

00:01:40.953 --> 00:01:42.953
into the document unchanged.

00:01:42.953 --> 00:01:47.273
In the demo corpus, 60 tag tests from a fictional webshop,

00:01:47.273 --> 00:01:49.353
this one matches 36.

00:01:50.033 --> 00:01:51.113
Then materialize.

00:01:51.673 --> 00:01:54.913
The filter is compiled against the catalog snapshot and the resulting

00:01:54.913 --> 00:01:56.813
list of IDs is written into the document.

00:01:57.373 --> 00:01:59.613
This is the step that makes a run reproducible.

00:02:00.173 --> 00:02:01.973
The filter stays for provenance.

00:02:02.553 --> 00:02:04.813
The embedded list is what actually runs.

00:02:05.793 --> 00:02:07.353
The result is the run spec.

00:02:07.913 --> 00:02:11.833
Versioned YAML JSON isomorphic with a published schema.

00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:17.433
A run ID minted at composed time, the correlation key for everything that

00:02:17.433 --> 00:02:23.653
follows, the selection and its materialized list, the source snapshot, the result

00:02:23.653 --> 00:02:26.973
format to expect, and a per run ingest token.

00:02:27.933 --> 00:02:29.853
The core sections are generic and closed.

00:02:30.393 --> 00:02:34.633
Exactly, one section is open, runner, and the core never looks inside it.

00:02:35.767 --> 00:02:41.187
Now, the part the whole design exists to make possible, runcomposer does not need to reach your test machines.

00:02:41.767 --> 00:02:45.887
No credentials on them, no network route, no agent it controls.

00:02:46.447 --> 00:02:49.547
It hands out a document and something on the other side runs it.

00:02:50.487 --> 00:02:51.147
Three ways.

00:02:51.727 --> 00:03:02.727
In process, the robot-pool runner executes the tests itself with partition fan out, duration balance chunking, and live verdicts streaming from an injected listener while the run is still going.

00:03:03.707 --> 00:03:05.227
Your own agent anywhere.

00:03:05.227 --> 00:03:10.687
runcomposer exec is one self-contained, standard library-only Python file.

00:03:11.347 --> 00:03:12.507
Copy it next to your code.

00:03:13.147 --> 00:03:20.147
It reads the spec as JSON, runs your command against exactly the listed IDs, and writes a correlation marker beside the output.

00:03:20.787 --> 00:03:21.667
Nothing to install.

00:03:22.707 --> 00:03:23.847
Or a CI job.

00:03:24.287 --> 00:03:31.887
The ci-trigger runner drives an existing parameterized job whose own stage runs that same vendored file and posts the bundle back.

00:03:31.887 --> 00:03:35.267
Whatever executes owes exactly three things.

00:03:35.267 --> 00:03:38.767
Execute the materialized list, not the filter.

00:03:38.767 --> 00:03:41.507
Executors do not recompile selections.

00:03:41.507 --> 00:03:42.927
Check for drift.

00:03:42.927 --> 00:03:47.387
If the live catalog hash differs from the one in the spec, refuse by default.

00:03:47.387 --> 00:03:50.327
And reference the run ID in the results.

00:03:51.007 --> 00:03:52.467
Three obligations.

00:03:53.207 --> 00:03:53.867
One document.

00:03:54.527 --> 00:03:58.087
Everything else, including the entire runner section, may be ignored.

00:03:58.087 --> 00:04:09.847
Continue copy again.

00:04:10.027 --> 00:04:18.107
ρέ tagged fingers across court line row OR

00:03:59.367 --> 00:04:01.767
Results come back decoupled from dispatch.

00:04:02.307 --> 00:04:08.387
Three transports, one pipeline, an HTTP push guarded by the run's own ingest token,

00:04:08.947 --> 00:04:14.387
a watched file drop directory for get transported or air gapped bundles, and

00:04:14.387 --> 00:04:17.447
plain runcomposer ingest from the command line.

00:04:18.407 --> 00:04:20.087
The bundle is just a directory.

00:04:20.667 --> 00:04:24.247
Commit it to a results branch, rsync it, attach it to a build.

00:04:24.247 --> 00:04:30.307
The marker inside carries the run ID and a hash of the exact spec bytes that were handed out,

00:04:30.607 --> 00:04:33.067
so the transport is your business and none of ours.

00:04:33.647 --> 00:04:35.547
The marker is also the safety.

00:04:36.267 --> 00:04:40.667
A bundle whose hash does not match, or that claims a run nobody dispatched,

00:04:41.107 --> 00:04:43.007
does not quietly enter your history.

00:04:43.707 --> 00:04:48.927
It lands in a visible quarantine inbox for a human to attach, promote, or discard.

00:04:50.027 --> 00:04:53.007
Redelivery is expected, so the rules are explicit.

00:04:53.007 --> 00:04:55.987
A byte identical bundle is a no-op.

00:04:56.407 --> 00:04:59.867
A different bundle for the same shard replaces that shard's verdicts.

00:05:00.487 --> 00:05:04.947
Last writer wins, because a correction has to be able to turn a fail back into a pass.

00:05:05.967 --> 00:05:08.707
Verdicts are pass, fail, skip, error.

00:05:09.347 --> 00:05:12.867
When every declared shard has delivered, the run is complete.

00:05:13.567 --> 00:05:15.727
Completion is computed, never guessed.

00:05:16.933 --> 00:05:21.673
and the loop closes. Once runs accrue, history becomes a selection source.

00:05:22.253 --> 00:05:25.693
Ask for the failures of the latest completed run, and they resolve at

00:05:25.693 --> 00:05:29.753
composed time into a normal static reproducible spec with a record of how

00:05:29.753 --> 00:05:30.793
the list was derived.

00:05:31.753 --> 00:05:36.593
Latest means latest completed. A run still awaiting results is not silently

00:05:36.593 --> 00:05:40.873
treated as an answer. And on a fresh install, these features are simply dark,

00:05:41.113 --> 00:05:45.313
which the tool says out loud, rather than returning a confidently empty list.

00:05:45.313 --> 00:05:51.313
Everything specific is a plugin. The sources, the runners, the parsers, the store.

00:05:51.853 --> 00:05:56.933
The core knows items, tags, selections, specs, runs, and verdicts, and a guard

00:05:56.933 --> 00:06:01.133
test fails the build if core code so much as mentions a framework's vocabulary.

00:06:02.073 --> 00:06:06.013
runcomposer. Self-hosted MIT. One command to try.

00:06:06.933 --> 00:06:09.613
The interface is a document, not a protocol.
